<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Danisco seen meeting 96/97 target.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Danisco seen meeting 96/97 target.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish distiller and food producer Danisco A/S is likely to achieve its declared goal of a 10-12 percent rise in 1996/97 profits according to a Reuters forecast by eight analysts published on Friday.</p>
<p>The panel forecast average increases in pre-tax profit of 12.7 percent to 1.807 billion crowns, with net profit expected to be 12.3 percent up at 1.367 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The analysts were particularly optimistic about Danisco's Ingredients Division's prospects with improved performance also seen for Packaging, Sugar and Food &amp; Beverages units.</p>
<p>Danisco is to unveil its full year 1996/97 result on Wednesday June 25. The share traded three crowns up at 427</p>
<p>crowns at 1000 GMT on Friday.</p>
<p>FORECAST TABLE-DANISCO 1996/97 FULL YEAR RESULT-EIGHT ANALYSTS</p>
<p>(billions of Danish crowns, unless otherwise states)</p>
<p>1996/97		 low/high	   average	   95/96   pct change</p>
<p>Turnover	     17.255/17.821	 17.590	  16.186    +8.7%</p>
<p>Operating result    1.958/2.055	  2.002	    1.796   +11.5%</p>
<p>Pre-tax result	1.737/1.857	  1.807	    1.604   +12.7%</p>
<p>Net result	    1.333/1.390	  1.367	    1.218   +12.3%</p>
<p>EPS(Dkk)		 22.2/24.2	  23.3	     21.9	+6.4%</p>
<p>--Joern Nurkka, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969653</p>
